      "value": "@{58c6da4c23f8d63e1401d385|full_name}: Yeah, this would cause a lot of proliferation. And I think it is a separate situation/issue than what I outlined here.\n\n\"Spawn points should be portals themselves.\" Makes me think that maybe the elegant solution is to just link two portals. But that leaves out the ability to have a portal send you to a specific spot and *not* have a portal nearby to return. \n\nI believe just being able to set a destination spawn location and allowing content creators to decide how/if the return will work is a better solution.\n\nThere are also situations where a creator is not using the big blue VRC Portal to send someone to the next room. So forcing the use of the portal would be a regression in the currently available flexibility. (Scripts that teleport you onto a hidden portal)\n\nHaving to wait for a portal behind me to despawn so I can navigate past it in some situations would be a bummer too.\n\nTo be totally clear this request is purely for connecting worlds in a logical manner and has nothing to do with just generically joining the world.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
