      "value": "@{58d2df84430f4652e88c5666|full_name}: Imagine two rooms that have similar long paths on them. In Room A on one end, you have a portal linking to Room B at the corresponding end. At the other ends of Room A and B you have another set of linking portals. With the approach you have outlined, this would not be possible.\n\nI really think setting a destination spawn point ID on a portal would be the best, simplest, and most flexible approach for interconnected world building.\n\n-OwlBoy",
      "viewerReactions": null
